{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The platforms a business takes bookings or orders at instead of its inbox (doors_elsewhere, spec 0.9.0, ADR-031). id is the token a manifest's doors_elsewhere entry names as platform, and the name a network gives such a door as its type platform:<id>. A URL is on a platform when its host is one of hosts or a name under one, and it is the business's own page there: page path, a path other than /; page subdomain, a name under the host other than www; page any, either. own_site: the platform also serves the business's pages on the business's own domain, and a page there is named by its host, not by the platform. hosts were read from each platform's own public pages and help (source), without signing in. Delivery and booking marketplaces that take a share of each sale are not listed: a business may still name any https page of its own choosing, with no platform. tracking_params are the query parameters a door may not carry: a name ending in * is a prefix.",
